# Local overrides for Docker Compose.
#
#   cp .env.example .env     # then edit .env; .env is never committed
#
# Compose reads .env from the repo root and puts its values into the
# ${VAR:-default} placeholders of compose.yaml. Every line here is optional:
# leave it commented out and the default from docs/01 section 7 applies.
#
# Notes:
# - A variable exported in your shell wins over .env.
# - Go programs started with `go run` do NOT read this file; they only see
#   variables exported in the shell (docs/00 section 6).
# - This file holds no real secret. The MySQL passwords in compose.yaml are
#   local demo passwords (docs/03 section 12.4).

# --- Ports on your machine ------------------------------------------------
# Change one when another program already uses it ("address already in use").
# If you change a port, use the same port in the localhost variables you
# export for `go run`, for example MYSQL_DSN=...@tcp(localhost:3307)/...
# MYSQL_HOST_PORT=3306
# REDIS_HOST_PORT=6379
# PUBSUB_HOST_PORT=8085
# WIREMOCK_HOST_PORT=8080

# --- Application settings (docs/01 section 7) -----------------------------
# Values for the containers, so host names are the compose service names
# (mysql, redis, pubsub, wiremock), never localhost.
# MYSQL_DSN=app:app@tcp(mysql:3306)/pipeline?parseTime=true
# MYSQL_MAX_OPEN_CONNS=10
# REDIS_ADDR=redis:6379
# PUBSUB_EMULATOR_HOST=pubsub:8085
# PUBSUB_PROJECT_ID=demo
# PUBSUB_TOPIC=rows-to-process
# PUBSUB_SUBSCRIPTION=rows-worker
# IMPORT_BATCH_SIZE=500
# IMPORT_PARSERS=4
# RELAY_BATCH_SIZE=500
# RELAY_INTERVAL=1s
# PLATFORM_URL=http://wiremock:8080
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=true
# RATE_LIMIT_RPS=200
# CACHE_TTL=10m
# WORKER_MAX_OUTSTANDING=100
# MAX_ATTEMPTS=5
